# Custom Markdown documentation

When adding or changing **app-specific Markdown syntax** (beyond stock md-editor-rt / markdown-it / CommonMark), document it in the **same change**. Do not ship parser/renderer-only work without docs.

## What counts

- New markdown-it / marked / TipTap rules that introduce user-facing markup
- New wiki/shortcode tokens (e.g. `![[…]]`, `[[file:…]]`, `<pgbr/>`)
- HTML comment file formats that authors or exporters rely on (`<!-- note-cover -->`, `<!-- chat-msg -->`, …)
- Behavior changes to an existing custom syntax (options, caption rules, render output)

## What does not need a new doc

- Stock CommonMark / GFM / md-editor-rt builtins (KaTeX, Mermaid, task lists, …)
- Pure renderer tweaks with no markup (e.g. external link `target=_blank`)
- Sidecars that are not inline Markdown (e.g. `.sync.pb`)

## Where to write

| Step | Path |
|------|------|
| Feature doc | `docs/custom-markdown/<feature-kebab>.md` |
| Index row | `docs/custom-markdown/index.md` table |
| VitePress sidebar | `docs/.vitepress/config.ts` (`themeConfig.sidebar`) |
| Global plugin (if any) | `src/config/mdEditorConfig.js` + XSS whitelist as needed |

One concern per file. Reuse an existing file when extending that feature; add a new file for a new token/family.

## Doc checklist (each feature file)

1. **Syntax** — exact patterns and examples
2. **Spec (interop)** — enough for another Markdown engine to reimplement:
   - Grammar / regex
   - Parse algorithm + failure behavior
   - Value normalization (size, color, escapes)
   - Canonical HTML or structured output
   - Post-process rules (caption fold, unwrap, …)
   - Non-goals
3. **Options / attrs** — keys, units, escaping
4. **Implementation** — primary source paths (parser, plugin, UI)
5. Prefer **English** in Spec/code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt; overview may be KO or EN
6. Update shared conventions in `docs/custom-markdown/index.md` when adding cross-cutting rules (size, hex, placeholder `src`, …)

```text
❌ BAD — new `[[foo:]]` token in chat parser, no docs/
❌ BAD — markdown-it plugin only; Spec missing so other parsers cannot port
❌ BAD — examples only, no canonical HTML / normalize rules
✅ GOOD — docs/custom-markdown/foo.md (Syntax + Spec) + index.md + VitePress sidebar + plugin/parser
✅ GOOD — extend wiki-image.md Spec when adding a new ![[…]] option
```
